The DCU is the successor to and a [[Soft reboot (fiction)|soft reboot]] of the [[DC Extended Universe]] (DCEU). The DCEU film ''[[The Flash (film)|The Flash]]'' (2023) resets that franchise's [[Continuity (fiction)|continuity]], and the DCU largely discards the prior [[Canon (fiction)|canon]] while accommodating the inclusion of certain characters from the outgoing franchise.<ref name="DCUSlateGizmodo" /> Despite this, James Gunn said in January 2023 that a "rough memory" of events depicted in his DCEU projects, the film ''[[The Suicide Squad (film)|The Suicide Squad]]'' (2021) and the [[Peacemaker season 1|first season]] of its spin-off television series ''[[Peacemaker (TV series)|Peacemaker]]'' (2022), would remain in the DCU,<ref name="DCUSlateGizmodo" /> with specific moments from the DCEU deemed to be canon to the DCU if they are directly referenced in a DCU project.<ref name="DCEUMomentsCanon" /> ''The Suicide Squad'' was not initially [[Retroactive continuity|retroactively incorporated]] into the DCU;<ref name="DCEUMomentsCanon" /> however, Gunn stated in October 2026 that the majority of ''The Suicide Squad'' was canon to the DCU. He acknowledged that while some aspects may not accurately line up within the DCU timeline, he felt it was a more seamless inclusion than ''Peacemaker'' season 1.<ref name="GunnTSSCanon" /> The overall events of ''The Suicide Squad'' were acknowledged in the first season of the animated series ''[[Creature Commandos (TV series)|Creature Commandos]]'' (2024–25), the [[Peacemaker season 2|second season of ''Peacemaker'']] (2025),<ref name="DCEUMomentsCanon" /><ref name="Kinnaman" /><ref name="TotalFilmTimelineOrder" /> and the 2026 setting of ''[[Lanterns (TV series)|Lanterns]]'' (2026),<ref name="LanternsStarroTSS" /> with the former two set a few years after the film's events.<ref name="TotalFilmTimelineOrder" /> Both ''Creature Commandos'' and ''Peacemaker'' notably address the death of Rick Flag Sr.'s son [[Rick Flag (DC Extended Universe)|Rick Flag Jr.]] at the hands of Peacemaker during "[[Project Starfish (DC Extended Universe)|Project Starfish]]" at [[Corto Maltese (DC Comics)|Corto Maltese]],<ref name="DCEUMomentsCanon" /><ref name="Kinnaman" /> while ''Lanterns'' references [[Starro]], the basis of Project Starfish.<ref name="LanternsStarroTSS" /> ''Peacemaker'' also addresses Flag Jr.'s relationship with Dr. [[June Moone (DC Extended Universe)|June Moone / Enchantress]] from the DCEU film ''[[Suicide Squad (2016 film)|Suicide Squad]]'' (2016).<ref name="KinnamanEnchantress" /> A vision presented by [[Circe (DC Universe)|Circe]] in ''Creature Commandos'' season 1 depicts a potential apocalyptic-future Earth ruled by [[Gorilla Grodd (DC Universe)|Gorilla Grodd]] and Princess Ilana Rostovic.<ref name="TotalFilmTimelineOrder" />

''[[Clayface (film)|Clayface]]'' (2026) is the first DCU film not to be set in the chronological order of its release, taking place before the events of ''Creature Commandos'' and the first DCU film, ''[[Superman (2025 film)|Superman]]'' (2025).<ref name="GunnClayfaceTimeline" /><ref name="ClayfaceCCTimeline" /> That film establishes that [[Clark Kent (DC Universe)|Kal-El / Clark Kent]] emerged as Superman three years before the film's events, which occur in mid-2025, after arriving on Earth from the planet [[Krypton (comics)|Krypton]] three decades earlier.<ref name="MoTTimeline" /><ref name="SupermanOpeningText" /> [[Metahuman]]s emerged approximately 300 years before the film's events, with numerous superheroes being active during this period.<ref name="SupermanOpeningText" /><ref name="SupermanMuralHistory" /> On retroactively incorporating ''The Suicide Squad'' within the DCU canon, Gunn stated that there were some potential complications, such as that film's references to Superman. He clarified that while the film is believed to take place in 2021, it would need to occur around 2023 or 2024, after Superman's emergence, to line up with the timeline established in ''Superman''.<ref name="GunnTSSCanon2" />{{efn|A DCU timeline listing by ''[[Total Film]]'' places ''The Suicide Squad'' approximately 2–3 years before ''Superman''.<ref name="TotalFilmTimelineOrder" />}} ''Superman'' takes place after the events of ''Creature Commandos''{{'s}} first season. ''Peacemaker'' season 2 is set a month after ''Superman'',<ref name="GunnFirstThreeTimeline" /><ref name="PeacemakerS2SupermanTimeline" /> and "an unspecified amount of a couple of years" after its first season.<ref name="EWMay2025CoverStory" />{{efn|A DCU timeline listing by ''[[Total Film]]'' places ''Peacemaker'' season 2 six months after the first season.<ref name="TotalFilmTimelineOrder" />}} The majority of ''Peacemaker''{{'s}} first season is canon to the DCU, except for the [[cameo appearance]] of the [[Justice League (DC Extended Universe)|DCEU Justice League]], because that team had yet to be formed in the new continuity.<ref name="GunnPeacemakerS1Canon" /><ref name="GunnLoreyTHRDec2024" /> That team is replaced by the [[Justice Gang]] members from ''Superman''—[[Kendra Saunders (DC Universe)|Kendra Saunders / Hawkgirl]], [[Guy Gardner (DC Universe)|Guy Gardner / Green Lantern]], and [[Michael Holt (DC Universe)|Michael Holt / Mister Terrific]]—alongside Superman and [[Kara Zor-El (DC Universe)|Kara Zor-El / Supergirl]],<ref name="JusticeGangRetcon" /><ref name="JusticeGangRetcon2" /> with that scene and the rest of the first season taking place before the events of ''Superman''.<ref name="EWMay2025CoverStory" /><ref name="PeacemakerS2PreviouslyInDCU" />

''Peacemaker'' season 2 continues from the events of ''Superman'',<ref name="GunnPeacemakerS2TVLine" /> and introduces the concept of the [[Multiverse (DC Comics)|multiverse]] within the DCU through the "Quantum Unfolding Chamber" [[pocket universe]] technology that Lex Luthor uses in ''Superman'' to access [[Parallel universes in fiction|alternate dimensions]]; at least 100 realities exist within the DCU.<ref name="PeacemakerS2Multiverse" /> ''Peacemaker'' season 2 takes place between the main DCU dimension and [[Earth-X (DC Comics)|Earth-X]], an alternate reality where the United States is ruled by [[Nazis]] and features alternate versions of Peacemaker and other characters.<ref name="EarthX" /> That season also introduces the inter-dimensional prison [[Salvation (DC Universe)|Salvation]],<ref name="CheckmateSalvationOriginalPlans" /> and directly sets up the ''Superman'' follow-up film ''[[Man of Tomorrow (film)|Man of Tomorrow]]'' (2027).<ref name="MoTPeacemakerS2Setup" /> ''[[Supergirl (2026 film)|Supergirl]]'' (2026) takes place in between ''Superman'' and ''Man of Tomorrow'',<ref name="SupergirlTimeline" /> with the latter set in "real time" after ''Superman'', roughly occurring in mid-2027.<ref name="MoTTimeline" /> The second season of ''Creature Commandos'' will also take place after the events of ''Peacemaker'' season 2.<ref name="CCS2Timeline" /> ''Lanterns'' is primarily set in 2016 as well as 2026, with the events of ''Superman'' occurring between those two settings.<ref name="LanternsTimeline" /> ''[[The People v. Gorilla Grodd]]'' is set to take place primarily after the events of ''Man of Tomorrow'', with various other time periods also depicted.<ref name="TPvGGTimeline" />

